     "color": "#F6CF71",
     "genAi": false,
     "label": "",
     "width": 360,
     "height": 840,
     "inputs": [],
     "markdown": "---\nlabel:\n---\n## 1 · Load\nWe bring in three open datasets: parking tickets for commercial vehicles, precinct boundaries and loading zone signs. A small table adds how many people live in each precinct. Sign locations are converted into map coordinates."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "9444fa42-1eef-5fc5-9f89-0bbe9cbd22dc",
    "type": "note",
    "zIndex": -1,
    "position": {
     "x": 420,
     "y": 40
    },
    "data": {
     "name": "Note",
     "color": "#9EB9F3",
     "genAi": false,
     "label": "",
     "width": 540,
     "height": 840,
     "inputs": [],
     "markdown": "---\nlabel:\n---\n## 2 · Measure\nWe count what happens in each precinct: how many tickets were issued (demand) and how many legal loading zones exist (supply). Filters keep only our 10 precincts and the dates we care about. Change date_from and date_to in Variables to move the time window."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "a4029d49-ccc9-5354-9db8-2f66ae8619e5",
    "type": "note",
    "zIndex": -1,
    "position": {
     "x": 1000,
     "y": 40
    },
    "data": {
     "name": "Note",
     "color": "#8BE0A4",
     "genAi": false,
     "label": "",
     "width": 960,
     "height": 840,
     "inputs": [],
     "markdown": "---\nlabel:\n---\n## 3 · Combine and rate\nEverything goes into one table with one row per precinct. Then we divide by population: tickets per 1,000 residents and loading zones per 1,000 residents. Now small and large precincts can be compared fairly."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "26eb2853-6c2f-53e1-9730-1615a937f788",
    "type": "note",
    "zIndex": -1,
    "position": {
     "x": 2000,
     "y": 40
    },
    "data": {
     "name": "Note",
     "color": "#FE88B1",
     "genAi": false,
     "label": "",
     "width": 350,
     "height": 840,
     "inputs": [],
     "markdown": "---\nlabel:\n---\n## 4 · Score\nTwo numbers become one. The Priority index scores each precinct from 0 to 100: more tickets and fewer loading zones means more delivery pressure. The score is then attached back to the precinct shapes."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "b1f2dbfd-1225-584b-a5e3-3a669fc20b84",
    "type": "note",
    "zIndex": -1,
    "position": {
     "x": 2390,
     "y": 40
    },
    "data": {
     "name": "Note",
     "color": "#F89C74",
     "genAi": false,
     "label": "",
     "width": 320,
     "height": 840,
     "inputs": [],
     "markdown": "---\nlabel:\n---\n## 5 · Map\nThe last node builds a Builder map for you: precincts colored by pressure and loading zones as points. Run again after a change and the map updates."
    }
   }
